-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Two notes, because the default matters here
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. OWNERSHIP. The copyright line above names DataGateways as the client the work was commissioned
   for. Whether copyright actually vests in the client or in the contractor depends on the
   engagement agreement, and this file is not that agreement. Confirm it against the contract and
   correct this line if it is wrong.

2. WHY NOT MIT. A permissive licence on a company's own marketing site would let anyone republish
   it verbatim, branding and all. "All rights reserved" is the safe default for client work and
   can always be relaxed later; the reverse is much harder.

